exports[`rhachet roles — a subject-mode role modded via .agent/repo=.mods given: [case1] a repo that mods a linked subject-mode package role when: [t1] the not-ed skill is run then: the not-found stderr matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"
✋ ConstraintError: no skill "fins.check" found — a mod in this repo nots it

  - .agent/repo=.mods/role=surfer/boot.yml nots skills/fins.check.sh (of test/surfer)

fix: drop the path from the mod's \`not:\` to run the published skill, or ship a skill of that path in the mod dir to shadow it

{
  "input": {
    "slugSkill": "fins.check"
  },
  "nots": [
    {
      "role": "surfer",
      "target": {
        "repo": "test",
        "role": "surfer"
      },
      "path": "skills/fins.check.sh",
      "modSpecPath": ".agent/repo=.mods/role=surfer/boot.yml"
    }
  ]
}

[args] run,--skill,fins.check

"
`;

